course: dictionary
lesson: 5480
title: One word, many meanings: latch
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A latch is a simple metal bar or catch that keeps a door or gate shut. «Latch the gate so the dog can't get out» tells you what to do: close it so it stays closed. When you see latch as a verb, it means to close something with a latch.
explain: Latch can also be a verb meaning to grab and hold tightly. «The cookiecutter shark is only about 50 centimetres long; it latches on with sucking lips» shows a small shark holding on very firmly to a much bigger animal. Read the words around latch, and they show you which meaning fits.
explain: The word also appears in phrases. «The door was on the latch» means it was shut but not locked. A «latchkey kid» is a child who lets themselves into an empty home after school. Phrases do not always follow the everyday meaning, so look at the whole sentence.
fact: A latch is a simple metal bar or catch that keeps a door or gate shut.
fact: «Latch» can also be a verb: to latch a gate means to close it with a latch.
fact: «To latch on to something» means to grab and hold it tightly, or to start following or understanding an idea.
fact: «A latchkey kid» is a child who lets themselves into an empty home after school.
fact: «Pool gates must self-latch» is an important safety rule: the gate shuts and catches by itself.
exercise: «Latch the gate so the dog can't get out.» What does latch mean here? | *Close a gate with a catch that keeps it shut | Open it wide so the dog can run | Dig a hole under it | Paint it a bright colour
exercise: «The cookiecutter shark latches on with sucking lips.» What does latches on mean? | Sings loudly to the whales | Swims away very quickly | Lets go and drifts off | *Grabs and holds tightly
exercise: «The raccoon can open bin lids, jars and even door latches.» What are door latches? | *Metal catches that keep doors shut | Paint colours used on doors | Kinds of food for raccoons | Tiny animals that live in doors
test: «Ella is a latchkey kid, so she lets herself in after school.» What does latchkey kid mean? | A child who fixes gates | A child who is poorly and stays in bed | *A child who lets themselves into an empty home after school | A child who loves keys
test: «The door was on the latch, so we could push it open.» What does on the latch mean? | Locked with a key | *Shut but not locked | Painted green | Wide open and broken
exam: «A baby latches on to feed.» What does latches on mean here? | *Attaches its mouth to the breast to feed | Cries loudly for milk | Falls fast asleep | Sits up and looks around
